-->

# AGENTS.md

<!-- 1–2 lines. What this is + the stack. No history, no marketing. -->
<Project name>: <one-line purpose>. <Language/framework/runtime + versions>, <package manager>.

## Commands

<!-- Exact, copy-pasteable commands. This is the most valuable section. Include the
     non-obvious flags and the fast/scoped variants agents should prefer. -->
- Install: `<cmd>`
- Dev server: `<cmd>` (port <n>)
- Test one file: `<cmd> path/to/file`   ← prefer this while iterating
- Test all: `<cmd>`
- Lint + typecheck: `<cmd>`
- Format: `<cmd>`
<!-- If something needs setup first (env var, local DB, docker, codegen), say so here:
     - Requires `<ENV_VAR>`; copy `.env.example` to `.env`.
     - Run `<codegen cmd>` after changing `<schema file>`. -->

## Definition of done

<!-- The checks an agent must run before saying it's finished. Agents will actually run these. -->
Before finishing any change, run and pass:
1. `<lint/typecheck cmd>`
2. `<tests for the touched area>`
3. <any other check, e.g. `<build cmd>` if you touched config>

## Where things live

<!-- NOT a directory tree or file-by-file tour (agents can `ls`). Only boundaries and
     non-obvious placements that an agent would otherwise get wrong. -->
- <New API endpoints go in `src/...`; register them in `src/.../routes.ts`>
- <`generated/` is codegen output — never edit by hand; regenerate with `<cmd>`>
- <Shared UI components: `packages/ui`; app-specific ones stay in the app>

## Conventions

<!-- Only rules that differ from language/framework defaults, or that a linter can't enforce.
     Pair every "don't" with a "do" (and a path to the thing to use instead). -->
- Don't <X>; use <Y> in `<path>` instead.
- <Domain rule, e.g. "Money is integer cents (`Money` type in `src/lib/money.ts`), never floats.">
- Follow the pattern in `<path/to/canonical/example.ts>` when adding a <thing>.

